        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Billy Corgan, James Iha, D'arcy Wretzky, Jimmy Chamberlin\n- Organizations: The Smashing Pumpkins, Greek Fire, Constantinople Records\n- Places: Chicago, Illinois; St. Louis, Missouri\n\nFacts:\n- In 1988, Billy Corgan and guitarist James Iha formed The Smashing Pumpkins in Chicago, Illinois.\n- The Smashing Pumpkins quickly gained momentum after D'arcy Wretzky joined as bassist and Jimmy Chamberlin joined as drummer.\n- Greek Fire is an American rock band from St. Louis, Missouri.\n- Constantinople Records is a record label created by Billy Corgan of The Smashing Pumpkins.",
